:"B","text":"B"},{"key":"C","text":"C"}]}]},{"id":"r3","index":3,"title":"Working From Home","instruction":"Read the article and choose the correct answer.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"Since 2020, millions of office workers have discovered the benefits of working from home. Many report saving over an hour a day on commuting."},{"label":"B","text":"However, managers worry that creativity suffers when teams rarely meet. Some companies now require staff to come in at least three days a week."},{"label":"C","text":"Researchers suggest that the best model depends on the task: focused work at home, collaboration in the office."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-15","number":15,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What benefit do many workers mention?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Higher pay"},{"key":"B","text":"Less commuting"},{"key":"C","text":"Better equipment"}]},{"id":"r-16","number":16,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Managers are concerned about","options":[{"key":"A","text":"costs"},{"key":"B","text":"creativity"},{"key":"C","text":"security"}]},{"id":"r-17","number":17,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Some companies now ask staff to come in","options":[{"key":"A","text":"once a week"},{"key":"B","text":"three days a week"},{"key":"C","text":"every day"}]},{"id":"r-18","number":18,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Researchers believe the best model","options":[{"key":"A","text":"depends on the task"},{"key":"B","text":"is fully remote"},{"key":"C","text":"is fully in the office"}]},{"id":"r-19","number":19,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Focused work is best done","options":[{"key":"A","text":"at home"},{"key":"B","text":"in the office"},{"key":"C","text":"in cafés"}]},{"id":"r-20","number":20,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The writer’s attitude is","options":[{"key":"A","text":"critical"},{"key":"B","text":"balanced"},{"key":"C","text":"enthusiastic"}]},{"id":"r-21","number":21,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The best title for the article is","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The End of Offices"},{"key":"B","text":"Finding the Right Balance"},{"key":"C","text":"Why Commuting Matters"}]}]},{"id":"r4","index":4,"title":"The Quiet Revolution of Urban Beekeeping","instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information in the text?","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"Over the past decade, beehives have appeared on rooftops, balconies and school grounds in cities around the world."},{"label":"B","text":"Supporters argue that urban hives help pollinate parks and gardens, while also teaching residents about nature."},{"label":"C","text":"Early studies suggested rooftop hives would struggle, yet the opposite proved true. City bees often produce more honey than their rural counterparts, largely because parks offer a longer flowering season.","highlight":"City bees often produce more honey than their rural counterparts"},{"label":"D","text":"Not everyone is convinced. Ecologists warn that a sudden rise in managed hives may crowd out wild pollinators."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-22","number":22,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Urban beehives can only be found on rooftops."},{"id":"r-23","number":23,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Rooftop hives yield less honey than hives in the countryside."},{"id":"r-24","number":24,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Parks have a longer flowering season than farmland."},{"id":"r-25","number":25,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Most city residents support urban beekeeping."},{"id":"r-26","number":26,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Some ecologists are worried about wild pollinators."}]},{"id":"r5","index":5,"title":"The Science of Habits","instruction":"Read the text and choose the correct answer.","passage":[{"label":"A","text":"Psychologists estimate that around forty percent of our daily actions are habits rather than conscious decisions."},{"label":"B","text":"Every habit follows a loop: a cue, a routine and a reward. Changing the routine while keeping the cue and reward is the most reliable way to break a bad habit."},{"label":"C","text":"Contrary to popular belief, forming a new habit takes on average sixty-six days, not twenty-one."}],"questions":[{"id":"r-27","number":27,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"About what share of daily actions are habits?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"20%"},{"key":"B","text":"40%"},{"key":"C","text":"60%"}]},{"id":"r-28","number":28,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"A habit loop consists of","options":[{"key":"A","text":"two parts"},{"key":"B","text":"three parts"},{"key":"C","text":"four parts"}]},{"id":"r-29","number":29,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"To break a bad habit, you should change the","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cue"},{"key":"B","text":"routine"},{"key":"C","text":"reward"}]},{"id":"r-30","number":30,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Forming a new habit takes on average","options":[{"key":"A","text":"21 days"},{"key":"B","text":"45 days"},{"key":"C","text":"66 days"}]},{"id":"r-31","number":31,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The “21 days” idea is described as","options":[{"key":"A","text":"accurate"},{"key":"B","text":"a popular belief"},{"key":"C","text":"a new finding"}]},{"id":"r-32","number":32,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The text is mainly about","options":[{"key":"A","text":"how habits work"},{"key":"B","text":"healthy eating"},{"key":"C","text":"memory"}]},{"id":"r-33","number":33,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The word “reliable” is closest to","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fast"},{"key":"B","text":"dependable"},{"key":"C","text":"difficult"}]},{"id":"r-34","number":34,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Who made the estimate in paragraph A?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Doctors"},{"key":"B","text":"Psychologists"},{"key":"C","text":"Teachers"}]},{"id":"r-35","number":35,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The writer would most likely agree that","options":[{"key":"A","text":"habits cannot change"},{"key":"B","text":"change takes time"},{"key":"C","text":"rewards are useless"}]}]}],"writing":[{"id":"w1","index":1,"label":"Task 1","kind":"Letter","prompt":"You recently stayed at a hotel and left something in your room. Write a letter to the manager. Describe the item and explain how it can be returned to y